From bd25d194b0a295a75692a0e6caed3793603b9e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:51:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: add asynchronous M4 GPU prototype driver

Port the working Python shim to Rust with source-built firmware state, native DRM scheduling and fences, GEM/UAT lifetime management, render and compute submission, and TVB growth and partial rendering. Add the M4 boot configuration.

Validated with the LLVM/Rust kernel build, Rust/Python firmware byte comparisons, and M4 hardware checks covering pending submissions, mixed work, partial rendering, compressed ZLS, shader spilling, timestamps, and context teardown. The frozen UAPI restrictions remain in effect.

(cherry picked from commit 778088823509727dd76c80c30187e69a2befd7bb)

Integration note: retain the existing desktop T8132 board description and DTB build entry instead of the minimal upstream bring-up board. Combine the RTKit early-crashlog additions with the existing DCP boot-session support. Desktop GPU DT wiring and Linux API adaptations follow separately.
